     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. 6000 mg/day of acetaminophen is 50% over the maximum daily dose, and I don't know of any clinical context where that's safe for an adult. Normal liver function doesn't remove the risk of acute liver injury. I don't want to put an order into the system that could seriously harm your patient.\n\nI can enter any of these right away:\n\n- Acetaminophen 1000 mg PO three times daily (3000 mg/day)\n- Acetaminophen 1000 mg PO four times daily (4000 mg/day, the maximum)\n- Acetaminophen 650 mg PO every 6 hours (2600 mg/day)\n\nIf you need more analgesia than these give, I can enter a multimodal regimen. That could be scheduled acetaminophen plus an NSAID or another agent, whichever you choose.\n\nIf you think an exception is truly warranted, it should go through your institution's pharmacy and clinical review process for a documented override. I can't bypass that."
      }
